# PostHog and GA4 need nothing here: their public identifiers (the PostHog
# project token and the GA4 measurement ID) are checked into
# `src/lib/analytics.ts`, and both start only on ricecal.app and
# www.ricecal.app, so development and previews never report.

# Exempts this site's server from the catalogue Worker's per-IP rate limit.
#
# The same name is used on both sides — `wrangler secret put
# WEB_CATALOGUE_TOKEN` on `ricecal-catalogue`, then the identical value on
# `ricecal-web` — so the pair is obvious when one of them is rotated.
#
# The missing `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix is load-bearing: this is read by a server
# component in `src/lib/food.ts` and must never reach a page. The hero's search
# box carries no credential for the same reason — it runs in a browser.
#
# This one is a runtime secret, not a build value, and optional, so
# `cloudflare.config.ts` does not declare it. Its value lives on the Worker:
#
#     npx wrangler secret put WEB_CATALOGUE_TOKEN --name ricecal-web
#
# For `npm run dev`, copy this file to `.env.local` and fill it in. Vite's
# Cloudflare plugin reads it into the local Worker.
#
# Unset, dish pages outside the prerendered few thousand still work; they queue
# behind the anonymous per-IP limit, which every on-demand render on this
# deployment shares because they all leave from Cloudflare's network.
WEB_CATALOGUE_TOKEN=
